{"title":"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 50","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_50&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e4bd655524e3e4f7af8c8fa168972f4b69d74f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\overline{CA} = \\overline{CB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"147\" height=\"19\" />. On <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is constructed away from the triangle. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of degrees in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1fc15d59287d2ff7bf581a84f348b3207a0c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c93af53c42c11cb817d4bc47c054c23e5ebf320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ x\\text{ depends upon }\\triangle ABC \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ x\\text{ is independent of the triangle} \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ x\\text{ may equal }\\angle CAD \\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ x\\text{ can never equal }\\angle CAB \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ x\\text{ is greater than }45^{\\circ}\\text{ but less than }90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"512\" height=\"77\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_50&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0aeca19b59a2a8b771d48d73a4c2f2d93eae8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB = \\angle CBA = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e192858cc0aed03b2b5fc79b273cf545c99e1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - 2A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is a square built on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/48247fddc37effb200c15278e2295cfea7a0ee51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = CB = CA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de20e3c47600377f5978eda980b408cb9322c185.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCD = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b157cd9ce8f07e2888b3a4b60526ba67f0759f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA = CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The vertex angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63fe9dbec0c29a1c8f19d9d36b6254827c242df3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle ACD = \\angle ACB + \\angle BCD = (180^\\circ - 2A) + 90^\\circ = 270^\\circ - 2A\\]\" width=\"485\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>In isosceles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, the base angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f105551f628f107282e0cc6c89063f3c1faece9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b7cd4095d58254f8d2c83e36e8990d020db4b58.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CAD = \\frac{180^\\circ - (270^\\circ - 2A)}{2} = \\frac{2A - 90^\\circ}{2} = A - 45^\\circ\\]\" width=\"418\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa7d066abb865686f0ba5cec05d41f8a411c7e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB = \\angle CAB - \\angle CAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"217\" height=\"16\" />, we find:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b291d645219b04f92f65b1ca18eb66676558a3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = A - (A - 45^\\circ) = 45^\\circ\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b85256d8a4fa3fa56ef839cc003fb32647de9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> is constant, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is independent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, which corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b796948f763471dad529946914e565390e3b9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_50&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME\" title=\"1956 AHSME\">1956 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1956 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1956\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 49\">Problem 49</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1956_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1956 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\"